<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
  <!--
    Access WiFi Information. Required by `NEHotspotNetwork.fetchCurrent()`, which HomeNetwork uses
    to read the current SSID for layer 1 of the connection model's home detection (see
    docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-havenapp-connection-model-design.md §4.1).

    This is an *accelerator only*. Without it — and without Location Services authorization, which
    is also required and is never requested during onboarding — `fetchCurrent` yields nil, the SSID
    is "unknown", and connection ordering falls through to the network path class and the 2s local
    probe. The app is fully correct in that state.

    NOTE FOR DEVICE BUILDS: this capability must be enabled on the App ID in the Apple Developer
    portal (it generally requires paid-program membership). Builds here run with
    CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO and therefore cannot verify that it is provisionable for this team. If
    signing fails with a missing-entitlement error, remove the CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS line from
    project.yml and re-run `xcodegen generate` — nothing else depends on it, and the SSID layer
    simply stays unavailable.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info</key><true/>
</dict></plist>
